    "canonical_id": "FIO_2001_SEC_15",
    "display_name": "Section 15",
    "title": "Sale of mortgaged property without intervention of Court",
    "verbatim_text": "(1) In this section, 'mortgaged property' means any immoveable property mortgaged by a customer or mortgagor in favour of a financial institution as security for finance.\n(2) Where a customer commits default, the financial institution may send three notices demanding payment and upon non-compliance, proceed to sell the mortgaged property by public auction without intervention of court.",
